  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscRC 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'During a research meeting, scientists discuss new treatment ideas while
    the clinical team outlines the information needed for a future trial. You take
    notes, ask clarifying questions, and highlight details that will matter later
    if the research moves forward.


    <b>As the research coordinator, what is
    your role in this situation?</b>'
  explanation: "Research coordinators help connect scientists and clinical teams
    so everyone stays informed and prepared as new ideas move forward. They don\u2019t
    design lab tests, write trial plans on their own, or decide which patients will
    participate; instead, they focus on clear communication and careful documentation
    so that, when the research is ready for next steps, the right information is
    already in place."
  correctAnswer: Acting as a bridge between the scientists and the clinical team
    to support communication and plan for future trials
  incorrectAnswer1: Deciding which safety tests the scientists should run on the
    new treatment in the lab
  incorrectAnswer2: Writing the scientific protocol, or study plan, that will be
    used in future clinical trials
  incorrectAnswer3: Making early decisions about which patients will be recruited
    to join the clinical trial
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: MulitpleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
